" :answer/id #uuid "3d6577ce-7c47-5a22-9728-0eee38cd2459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=8\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136400/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer/id #uuid "150fd6c2-e160-563d-878f-591465fd74c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136400/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf7d35c-0b84-5983-9a9d-9de99b8d986a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-136400/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer-field/choices ["q-136400/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-136400/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" "q-136400/selection/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" "q-136400/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" "q-136400/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-136400" :question/id #uuid "6cfb09c2-0cab-57af-9ddd-621d3a23bf89" :question/math-academy-id "q-136400" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i-4j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-4i+16j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(8i-8j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=2i-4j,\\,u=-4i+16j,\\,v=8i-8j\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 8i-8j & =(-4i+16j)+(2i-4j)t \\\\ 12i-24j & =(2i-4j)t \\\\ 12i-24j & =2ti-4tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12 & = & 2t \\\\ -24 & = & -4t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=6\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-136400/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "a814644e-e7d3-5580-b29c-d71dc4b9fc98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "cf0c6569-b17d-53b0-9d11-9321cd6b03de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9864669d-3663-5efa-b110-21c72e4f012f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317185/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-317185/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-317185/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9affb070-f3c9-5f0d-9ebf-43598baf8c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "081175e1-2b61-51d8-b6bf-b68234096e27" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317185/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-317185/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317185" :question/id #uuid "11197922-a96a-5072-b8ff-cc32fcc9cbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-317185" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(i-7j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(3i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=3\\,\\text{h}.$\n\n$v=($\n{{field-1}}$i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$j\\,)\\,\\text{km/h}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=i-7j,\\,a=3i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(i-7j)+(3i+4j)(3) \\\\  & =(i-7j)+(9i+12j) \\\\  & =(10i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317185/field-1" "q-317185/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317185"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-318175/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "fb5a26e2-2468-55fc-9ae3-56365d3b6ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318175/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0144c6fc-5965-5547-a520-3215bcbf44f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-318175/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-318175/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-318175/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7b1865dc-50a4-52ad-be53-ba23d0f19328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318175/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5b10fb1-4166-5235-a379-9f20ca2e7746" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-318175/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-318175/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-318175" :question/id #uuid "8dc28f9d-6ed1-5ee4-af68-b721264477e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-318175" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. The velocity of the particle equals $(9i-4j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ both when $t=0\\,\\text{h}$ and $t=5\\,\\text{h}.$ What is the acceleration of the particle?\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=9i-4j,\\,v=9i-4j,\\,t=5\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 9i-4j & =(9i-4j)+a(5) \\\\ 0 & =5a \\\\ a & =(0\\,i+0\\,j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-318175/field-1" "q-318175/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-318175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
